Publish max_cpus from machine_lockdown() and trace the way into bsd_init()

With eight ADT cpu nodes the boot now reaches machine_lockdown() and stops
there: SweetCPU::finishStart() is the only caller of ml_set_max_cpus() on
this variant, and it runs from an IOKit start() that has not happened yet,
so ml_wait_max_cpus() never wakes. Publish the value here, which is what the
non-VINCE path already does, and print the two remaining milestones so the
next stall shows up on the framebuffer console.

--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
@@ -561,4 +561,9 @@
 #if !defined(VINCE) || !defined(TULIP_SMP)
         ml_set_max_cpus(machine_info.max_cpus);
 #endif
+#if defined(VINCE) && defined(TULIP_SMP)
+        /* SweetCPU publishes max_cpus from an IOKit start() that runs after this point,
+         * so nothing would ever wake ml_wait_max_cpus(). Publish it here instead. */
+        ml_set_max_cpus(machine_info.max_cpus);
+#endif
 }
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -788,3 +789,4 @@
 #ifdef  MACH_BSD
+	printf("TULIP BOOT: before bsd_init\n");
 	bsd_init();
 #endif
